    "introduction": "BP produces and trades oil and natural gas and supplies fuels and other energy products to businesses and consumers. Its operations connect upstream production with refining, wholesale trading, service stations, convenience retail and products such as Castrol lubricants. It also participates in electricity, charging and other energy activities. Earnings arise at several stages of the supply chain, including selling resources, processing crude oil and serving end customers. These activities have different sensitivities to energy prices and demand. The business requires substantial spending on infrastructure, maintenance and new projects, making operating efficiency, project selection and the balance between investment and cash generation important features.",
